      "message": "fix(tofu): pin federated cred issuer to current cluster URL (cross-sub workaround)\n\nFollow-up to #37. That PR switched the federated identity credential's\n`issuer` to `data.azurerm_kubernetes_cluster.infra.oidc_issuer_url`,\nexpecting to read the live value from the cluster. But the AKS cluster\nlives in subscription 606a1ca1 (\"romaine-life\"), while this tofu stack\nauthenticates to aee0cbd2 (\"Azure subscription 1\"); the data source\n404s and apply fails — same failure as diagrams/tofu has been hitting\nsince 2026-04-30.\n\nCross-sub Reader on the CI principal is the right long-term fix, owned\nby infra-bootstrap. Until then, restore the variable and update its\ndefault to the cluster's current value (`…/5aced6d5-…`). Apply now\nsucceeds and the federated cred gets re-issued with the correct URL,\nunblocking pod startup.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e",
